1
00:00:00,417 --> 00:00:02,167
<i>Previously on "The Ark"...</i>

2
00:00:02,168 --> 00:00:03,585
I always thought
Black Thorn was a rumor.

3
00:00:03,586 --> 00:00:06,046
<i>This is a genetic library
of selected</i>

4
00:00:06,047 --> 00:00:07,798
<i>animalia DNA samples
from Earth.</i>

5
00:00:07,799 --> 00:00:10,217
<i>You did all of this
in your sleep?</i>

6
00:00:10,218 --> 00:00:11,510
<i>Everyone on Homebase
loves you.</i>

7
00:00:11,511 --> 00:00:12,678
<i>And I love you.</i>

8
00:00:12,679 --> 00:00:13,762
I love you too.

9
00:00:13,763 --> 00:00:14,972
I saw an opportunity
when I detected

10
00:00:14,973 --> 00:00:16,223
<i>the dormant chip,
so I took it.</i>

11
00:00:16,224 --> 00:00:18,475
That thing put you
in my head, didn't it?

12
00:00:18,476 --> 00:00:20,602
We built a nice colony
called Homebase 1.

13
00:00:20,603 --> 00:00:21,687
Trail stops here.

14
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:23,105
There is indeed something
in that lake.

15
00:00:23,106 --> 00:00:25,190
It's "EF1."
Must have been shot down.

16
00:00:25,191 --> 00:00:26,608
What have you found?

17
00:00:26,609 --> 00:00:27,818
Bodies.

18
00:00:27,819 --> 00:00:29,446
There were survivors.

19
00:00:43,418 --> 00:00:46,170
Zed.

20
00:00:46,171 --> 00:00:48,630
I'm so sorry
about this, mate.

21
00:00:48,631 --> 00:00:51,717
We cross-referenced each
ID with the EF manifest.

22
00:00:51,718 --> 00:00:54,303
These bodies are from "EF1,"
but I'm relieved to say

23
00:00:54,304 --> 00:00:55,888
your son is not one of them.

24
00:00:55,889 --> 00:00:57,723
Don't be.

25
00:00:57,724 --> 00:01:00,559
My son's body is likely
at the bottom of that lake.

26
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:02,770
I really hope
that's not true.

27
00:01:02,771 --> 00:01:06,857
I want to know exactly
how my people died

28
00:01:06,858 --> 00:01:09,151
and who buried them.

29
00:01:09,152 --> 00:01:10,736
Is it possible
they were buried

30
00:01:10,737 --> 00:01:12,029
by other "EF1" survivors?

31
00:01:12,030 --> 00:01:14,406
I mean, maybe they're
still out there, alive.

32
00:01:14,407 --> 00:01:15,532
No.

33
00:01:15,533 --> 00:01:18,327
They would've come to us
as soon as we arrived.

34
00:01:18,328 --> 00:01:22,289
I've finished reviewing
the autopsy results.

35
00:01:22,290 --> 00:01:24,708
They have all been dead
for about 22 months,

36
00:01:24,709 --> 00:01:26,877
and they were killed
the same way...

37
00:01:31,007 --> 00:01:32,841
By gunshot.

38
00:01:57,826 --> 00:01:59,201
I want answers.

39
00:01:59,202 --> 00:02:01,120
We'll get them.
Dr. Marsh said the bodies--

40
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:03,122
What type of weapon
systems were used?

41
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:04,957
Ammunition?
What was the motive?

42
00:02:04,958 --> 00:02:07,376
Zed, Dr. Marsh said
the bodies died two years ago.

43
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:08,627
I'm aware of that.

44
00:02:08,628 --> 00:02:09,962
You know who arrived
here two years ago?

45
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:11,755
"Ark 11."

46
00:02:11,756 --> 00:02:13,632
You think this was
Ves and Black Thorn?

47
00:02:13,633 --> 00:02:14,758
Could be.

48
00:02:14,759 --> 00:02:16,135
This was the secret
she was hiding,

49
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:17,428
and Hammond found out.

50
00:02:17,429 --> 00:02:19,388
It would explain
why she killed him

51
00:02:19,389 --> 00:02:20,931
and framed Strickland.

52
00:02:20,932 --> 00:02:23,642
But does that mean
she shut down the "EF1" ship?

53
00:02:23,643 --> 00:02:25,477
If she did,

54
00:02:25,478 --> 00:02:27,813
the rest of "Ark 11" would
all be complicit.

55
00:02:27,814 --> 00:02:29,648
I trusted you, Garnet.

56
00:02:29,649 --> 00:02:32,026
I trusted that all
of the GSA would

57
00:02:32,027 --> 00:02:33,444
fall behind you
and choose peace.

58
00:02:33,445 --> 00:02:34,820
I'm sorry, Zed, but I--

59
00:02:34,821 --> 00:02:36,406
Captain Avega!

60
00:02:39,492 --> 00:02:42,619
Captain Avega, I can't
control the actions of others.

61
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:44,913
I didn't even know there was
a Black Thorn unit here.

62
00:02:44,914 --> 00:02:46,165
But I can tell you this.

63
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:48,125
If they or any other
GSA personnel are responsible

64
00:02:48,126 --> 00:02:51,128
for the murder of your people,

65
00:02:51,129 --> 00:02:53,047
they'll pay the consequences.

66
00:02:53,048 --> 00:02:54,131
How?

67
00:02:54,132 --> 00:02:55,424
We'll follow due process.

68
00:02:55,425 --> 00:02:57,342
Due process?
Are you kidding?

69
00:02:57,343 --> 00:03:00,387
More than 200 of my people
were murdered.

70
00:03:00,388 --> 00:03:02,723
A crime far beyond the scope

71
00:03:02,724 --> 00:03:06,226
of anything that would
require due process.

72
00:03:06,227 --> 00:03:07,978
For now, we need to
still make sure everyone

73
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:09,355
at Homebase is safe.

74
00:03:09,356 --> 00:03:11,732
"Ark 16" is disembarking
as we speak.

75
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:14,193
And we still don't know
who the Black Thorn are.

76
00:03:14,194 --> 00:03:16,612
Okay, let's start
by talking to Kimi.

77
00:03:16,613 --> 00:03:18,989
Since EF Hunters was
a division of Black Thorn,

78
00:03:18,990 --> 00:03:20,407
maybe she can help.

79
00:03:20,408 --> 00:03:22,242
I didn't know Kimi was
an EF hunter.

80
00:03:22,243 --> 00:03:24,411
This just keeps getting
better and better.

81
00:03:24,412 --> 00:03:26,121
This is when we were
still at war.

82
00:03:26,122 --> 00:03:28,832
Her job was
to murder people like me.

83
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:30,292
Again, we were at war.

84
00:03:30,293 --> 00:03:32,669
Since then, Kimi has more than
proven herself non-partisan.

85
00:03:32,670 --> 00:03:35,673
I would trust her
with my life and yours.

86
00:03:35,674 --> 00:03:37,007
Just the same,

87
00:03:37,008 --> 00:03:39,885
I don't want her
anywhere near me.

88
00:03:39,886 --> 00:03:42,012
Captain Avega,
why don't you go supervise

89
00:03:42,013 --> 00:03:44,390
the divers at the lake?

90
00:03:44,391 --> 00:03:45,933
You can help them identify
the rest of the bodies.

91
00:03:45,934 --> 00:03:49,312
Strickland and I will
handle everything else.

92
00:03:51,147 --> 00:03:52,523
Fine.

93
00:03:52,524 --> 00:03:55,401
But let me give you
a word of advice.

94
00:03:55,402 --> 00:03:58,946
Former EF security
are the only ones we know

95
00:03:58,947 --> 00:04:00,864
for sure are not Black Thorn.

96
00:04:00,865 --> 00:04:03,200
I will tell my men to follow

97
00:04:03,201 --> 00:04:06,286
yours and Felix's orders
while you investigate.

98
00:04:06,287 --> 00:04:07,913
But I would relieve

99
00:04:07,914 --> 00:04:11,543
all former GSA security
personnel of their duties.

100
00:04:19,509 --> 00:04:22,219
Hey.

101
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:23,303
Where are you going?

102
00:04:23,304 --> 00:04:24,638
Uh, oh, um, I--

103
00:04:24,639 --> 00:04:26,432
Tell her you want
to stretch your legs.

104
00:04:26,433 --> 00:04:28,767
I'm just gonna go
and stretch my legs.

105
00:04:28,768 --> 00:04:30,978
Don't you wanna shower first?

106
00:04:30,979 --> 00:04:32,813
Rest? We just got home.

107
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:34,606
Don't you worry
about me, my love.

108
00:04:34,607 --> 00:04:36,775
I'm absolutely fine, okay?

109
00:04:36,776 --> 00:04:38,110
I am worried about you.

110
00:04:38,111 --> 00:04:39,778
You've been through a lot,
and you need to rest.

111
00:04:39,779 --> 00:04:41,071
You need to go now.

112
00:04:41,072 --> 00:04:42,281
You know what?

113
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:43,949
I'm--I'm actually
feeling kind of hungry.

114
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:46,201
So I'm just gonna head
down to Landing Pad,

115
00:04:46,202 --> 00:04:48,078
quickly grab something,
all right?

116
00:04:48,079 --> 00:04:49,580
Okay, I'll come with you.

117
00:04:49,581 --> 00:04:51,248
- Absolutely not.
- Uh, no.

118
00:04:51,249 --> 00:04:52,458
No, no, no. It's fine.

119
00:04:52,459 --> 00:04:53,917
It's fine.
You, uh--

120
00:04:53,918 --> 00:04:55,794
you wanna stay here
and get unpacked, get settled.

121
00:04:55,795 --> 00:04:59,631
So, uh, yeah, you stay here,
and I will be right back, okay?

122
00:04:59,632 --> 00:05:00,841
Mwah!

123
00:05:06,473 --> 00:05:08,265
Hey. Hey, listen.

124
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:09,850
You need to back off, okay?

125
00:05:09,851 --> 00:05:13,145
I can't think with you always
hovering and in my ear.

126
00:05:13,146 --> 00:05:14,396
You don't need to think.

127
00:05:14,397 --> 00:05:16,732
You need to do as I say.

128
00:05:16,733 --> 00:05:18,776
Something's
different about you.

129
00:05:18,777 --> 00:05:20,319
It's like you're--

130
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:22,071
you're deeper in my brain
or something.

131
00:05:22,072 --> 00:05:23,989
Follow me.

132
00:05:23,990 --> 00:05:25,532
Where are we going?

133
00:05:25,533 --> 00:05:27,826
To the part
of me that's sick.

134
00:05:27,827 --> 00:05:28,827
Come.

135
00:05:28,828 --> 00:05:30,079
Let me show you.

136
00:05:55,188 --> 00:05:56,523
Hi.

137
00:06:00,026 --> 00:06:01,027
Hi.

138
00:06:02,821 --> 00:06:04,113
You're back.

139
00:06:04,114 --> 00:06:05,239
Yeah.

140
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:06,532
Oh.

141
00:06:09,202 --> 00:06:10,452
I missed you.

142
00:06:10,453 --> 00:06:13,330
Oh, God, I missed you too.

143
00:06:13,331 --> 00:06:15,082
Really?

144
00:06:15,083 --> 00:06:16,125
Really.

145
00:06:24,467 --> 00:06:26,427
Uh, Sanji.

146
00:06:26,428 --> 00:06:27,637
Hmm?

147
00:06:29,597 --> 00:06:30,974
I've got to
tell you something.

148
00:06:38,023 --> 00:06:40,316
Milan is dead.

149
00:06:40,317 --> 00:06:42,568
What?

150
00:06:42,569 --> 00:06:43,861
You remember he had

151
00:06:43,862 --> 00:06:45,279
internal bleeding
when you left.

152
00:06:48,074 --> 00:06:49,283
Yeah, but--

153
00:06:49,284 --> 00:06:51,827
It was manageable at first,

154
00:06:51,828 --> 00:06:55,414
but things took a turn
for the worse quickly,

155
00:06:55,415 --> 00:06:56,999
and he coded.

156
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:01,755
We--we were unable
to resuscitate him.

157
00:07:04,299 --> 00:07:05,382
Come here.

158
00:07:13,391 --> 00:07:15,768
You okay?

159
00:07:15,769 --> 00:07:17,103
Um--

160
00:07:18,229 --> 00:07:20,022
You're relieved?

161
00:07:20,023 --> 00:07:20,940
Relieved?

162
00:07:22,567 --> 00:07:25,235
You think I'm relieved
that he's dead?

163
00:07:25,236 --> 00:07:26,612
No, no, of course not.

164
00:07:26,613 --> 00:07:28,322
That's not what I meant.

165
00:07:28,323 --> 00:07:30,032
I--

166
00:07:31,409 --> 00:07:32,910
I don't know.

167
00:07:32,911 --> 00:07:34,536
Um, what?

168
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:41,001
For the record,
I disavowed Black Thorn

169
00:07:41,002 --> 00:07:42,961
as soon as I was exposed
as an EF hunter.

170
00:07:42,962 --> 00:07:45,297
I've been loyal
solely to you, "Ark 1,"

171
00:07:45,298 --> 00:07:46,840
and Homebase ever since.

172
00:07:46,841 --> 00:07:47,966
We know.

173
00:07:47,967 --> 00:07:49,468
Do you know where
Ves might be hiding?

174
00:07:49,469 --> 00:07:50,761
No.

175
00:07:50,762 --> 00:07:52,096
I didn't even know
she was Black Thorn.

176
00:07:52,097 --> 00:07:53,681
As I understand it,
you were each relegated

177
00:07:53,682 --> 00:07:55,182
to a specific Ark?

178
00:07:55,183 --> 00:07:57,810
Yes, in isolated units
with our own codes.

179
00:07:57,811 --> 00:08:00,729
So have no idea who
"Ark 11's" other members are.

180
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:03,565
Did every ship have
the same number of Thorns?

181
00:08:03,566 --> 00:08:05,943
On "Ark 15," Lati and I
were the only ones.

182
00:08:05,944 --> 00:08:08,862
The larger groups
could be 12, 15.

183
00:08:08,863 --> 00:08:10,614
And they were all led
by commanders.

184
00:08:10,615 --> 00:08:12,116
- Like Ves?
- Mm-hmm.

185
00:08:12,117 --> 00:08:14,410
So whoever
the "Ark 11" members are...

186
00:08:14,411 --> 00:08:16,578
They're all loyal to Ves.

187
00:08:16,579 --> 00:08:19,707
Do you have any idea how
she was able to summon them all

188
00:08:19,708 --> 00:08:21,125
so quickly to help her escape?

189
00:08:21,126 --> 00:08:22,793
Every active-duty Thorn
keeps a small device

190
00:08:22,794 --> 00:08:24,461
on their person at all times,

191
00:08:24,462 --> 00:08:27,840
an encrypted beacon that can
summon all members of the unit.

192
00:08:27,841 --> 00:08:31,635
When triggered, all the other
Thorns meet at that location.

193
00:08:31,636 --> 00:08:33,887
So we should find
Ves and then--

194
00:08:33,888 --> 00:08:36,015
Use her beacon
to smoke out her team.

195
00:09:04,878 --> 00:09:06,336
Eva?

196
00:09:06,337 --> 00:09:07,588
Just get her out of here.

197
00:09:07,589 --> 00:09:09,048
You lied to me.

198
00:09:09,049 --> 00:09:10,257
No, I didn't.

199
00:09:10,258 --> 00:09:12,092
You said you were going
to a bar to get food.

200
00:09:12,093 --> 00:09:13,218
Eva, listen to me.

201
00:09:13,219 --> 00:09:14,345
You need to go, okay?

202
00:09:14,346 --> 00:09:15,804
You need to go now.

203
00:09:15,805 --> 00:09:16,930
You're scaring me.

204
00:09:16,931 --> 00:09:18,224
I want to bring
you to infirmary.

205
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:21,518
Listen to me.

206
00:09:21,519 --> 00:09:24,188
I've grown deeper
into your brain,

207
00:09:24,189 --> 00:09:27,900
and I can make you do
whatever I want.

208
00:09:27,901 --> 00:09:31,779
So tell her to leave.

209
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:33,280
You can't be here.

210
00:09:33,281 --> 00:09:36,408
Hey. It's me.

211
00:09:36,409 --> 00:09:38,577
You can talk to me.
- I can't.

212
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:40,537
I'm sorry it had
to come to this.

213
00:09:40,538 --> 00:09:43,374
Kill her.

214
00:09:43,375 --> 00:09:45,125
Now.

215
00:10:09,192 --> 00:10:11,068
It's okay.

216
00:10:12,445 --> 00:10:13,988
I'm so sorry.

217
00:10:13,989 --> 00:10:15,698
It's okay.

218
00:10:22,372 --> 00:10:24,498
I can't believe
what I'm seeing.

219
00:10:24,499 --> 00:10:25,749
What is it?

220
00:10:25,750 --> 00:10:27,334
You know how Maddox put
those chips in our brains

221
00:10:27,335 --> 00:10:29,211
when we first arrived here?

222
00:10:29,212 --> 00:10:31,213
Well, Brice's chip
has activated

223
00:10:31,214 --> 00:10:35,217
and become entangled in strands
of new neural tissue.

224
00:10:35,218 --> 00:10:37,428
It has to do with whatever
happened to me on Ross.

225
00:10:37,429 --> 00:10:39,471
Yeah, but your chip
looked completely normal

226
00:10:39,472 --> 00:10:41,807
after we rescued you,
which means the strands grew

227
00:10:41,808 --> 00:10:43,267
over the last few days.

228
00:10:43,268 --> 00:10:46,353
Maybe that explains
your behavior from today.

229
00:10:46,354 --> 00:10:49,023
Maybe the chip is
controlling you.

230
00:10:49,024 --> 00:10:50,399
So remove the chip.

231
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:52,568
Trust me, you don't
want to do that.

232
00:10:52,569 --> 00:10:54,820
We can't remove it now
without it killing you.

233
00:10:54,821 --> 00:10:56,113
I like her.

234
00:10:56,114 --> 00:10:58,949
But there must be a way
to shut down the chip.

235
00:10:58,950 --> 00:11:00,242
But how?

236
00:11:00,243 --> 00:11:01,368
I don't know.

237
00:11:01,369 --> 00:11:02,619
I wonder if Alicia could

238
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:04,830
help us tap into
the software somehow.

239
00:11:04,831 --> 00:11:06,373
Worth a try.

240
00:11:06,374 --> 00:11:08,000
Alicia to infirmary.

241
00:11:08,001 --> 00:11:09,418
It's urgent.

242
00:11:09,419 --> 00:11:13,172
None of them will
ever get me out.

243
00:11:13,173 --> 00:11:16,759
Leave now before I make
you hurt someone.

244
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:19,261
- Doc?
- Yeah?

245
00:11:19,262 --> 00:11:20,888
I need you to restrain me.

246
00:11:20,889 --> 00:11:22,389
- What?
- Sorry?

247
00:11:22,390 --> 00:11:24,600
Look, if your theory
is correct,

248
00:11:24,601 --> 00:11:26,769
I might not be able
to control my actions.

249
00:11:26,770 --> 00:11:27,936
Are you sure?

250
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:32,775
Do it.

251
00:11:32,776 --> 00:11:34,068
Fast.

252
00:11:34,069 --> 00:11:35,403
Okay.

253
00:11:37,238 --> 00:11:40,157
Hey, we're going
to figure this out.

254
00:11:40,158 --> 00:11:41,658
Oh, trust me, you're not.

255
00:11:49,376 --> 00:11:54,004
I always thought Black Thorn
was an old wives tale.

256
00:11:54,005 --> 00:11:55,130
Don't know anything about it.

257
00:11:55,131 --> 00:11:56,590
Why do you ask?

258
00:11:56,591 --> 00:11:58,008
Captain, we have
reason to believe

259
00:11:58,009 --> 00:11:59,510
that Ves Ilic was a commander

260
00:11:59,511 --> 00:12:01,261
of a Black Thorn unit
on your ship.

261
00:12:01,262 --> 00:12:03,138
- On "Ark 11"?
- Yes.

262
00:12:03,139 --> 00:12:04,264
There's no way.

263
00:12:04,265 --> 00:12:06,100
Why do you say that?

264
00:12:06,101 --> 00:12:07,935
I knew everything that
happened on that ship.

265
00:12:07,936 --> 00:12:10,979
Well, we think she
might have shot down "EF1."

266
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:12,398
How?

267
00:12:12,399 --> 00:12:14,483
"Ark 11" had no weapons.

268
00:12:14,484 --> 00:12:16,652
And it's not like
she could've secretly been

269
00:12:16,653 --> 00:12:20,781
hiding something big enough
to shoot down a whole ship.

270
00:12:20,782 --> 00:12:24,743
I'm sorry, but this all
just sounds ridiculous.

271
00:12:24,744 --> 00:12:25,953
Okay, then.

272
00:12:25,954 --> 00:12:28,414
Thank you for your time.

273
00:12:28,415 --> 00:12:29,957
We need to talk to Angus.

274
00:12:29,958 --> 00:12:31,792
Angus? Why?

275
00:12:36,673 --> 00:12:37,840
Angus.

276
00:12:37,841 --> 00:12:39,758
Have you found any evidence
of sunflowers

277
00:12:39,759 --> 00:12:41,093
growing here naturally?

278
00:12:41,094 --> 00:12:42,469
No.

279
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:44,805
Which is a bummer when you
think about their impact

280
00:12:44,806 --> 00:12:48,727
on soil health
and the biofuel potential.

281
00:12:49,978 --> 00:12:52,147
Let me just check the, uh--

282
00:12:56,943 --> 00:12:59,820
Doesn't look like any other
Arks carried them either.

283
00:12:59,821 --> 00:13:01,113
Why do you ask?

284
00:13:01,114 --> 00:13:05,701
Yeah, what do sunflowers
have to do with "EF1"?

285
00:13:05,702 --> 00:13:07,411
The former captain
of "Ark 11" was

286
00:13:07,412 --> 00:13:08,954
pruning sunflowers.

287
00:13:08,955 --> 00:13:11,540
If there aren't any here and
no one brought them on Earth,

288
00:13:11,541 --> 00:13:14,209
then where did he get them?

289
00:13:14,210 --> 00:13:16,503
You think he brought
them in the DNA vault?

290
00:13:16,504 --> 00:13:18,797
Uh, there's no vault
on "Ark 11."

291
00:13:18,798 --> 00:13:21,258
Yes, that's what
we wanted you to think.

292
00:13:21,259 --> 00:13:22,718
No one knows
the room even exists,

293
00:13:22,719 --> 00:13:24,762
which makes it a good place
for Ves to hide.

294
00:13:24,763 --> 00:13:26,055
Mm-hmm.

295
00:13:26,056 --> 00:13:28,182
Well, all the vaults were
built in the same place--

296
00:13:28,183 --> 00:13:30,851
behind the wall
in OT section of G Deck.

297
00:13:30,852 --> 00:13:33,729
Okay.

298
00:13:33,730 --> 00:13:37,649
"Ark 11's" G Deck
is now Building 14B.

299
00:13:37,650 --> 00:13:39,193
Let's go.

300
00:13:39,194 --> 00:13:40,652
Mr. Trust.

301
00:13:40,653 --> 00:13:42,946
The divers found
the server box from "EF1."

302
00:13:42,947 --> 00:13:45,199
Oh, hi.

303
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:46,450
Hi.

304
00:13:46,451 --> 00:13:48,619
Is the data salvageable?

305
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:49,578
Who knows?

306
00:13:49,579 --> 00:13:52,289
I'm sure as hell gonna try.

307
00:13:52,290 --> 00:13:53,791
Hopefully we'll find
the captain's log

308
00:13:53,792 --> 00:13:55,501
so we can learn
what really happened.

309
00:13:55,502 --> 00:13:56,668
Great.

310
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:59,254
Let me know the second
you find anything.

311
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:01,215
- Check it out.
- Uh-huh.

312
00:14:01,216 --> 00:14:03,717
- Let's go over there.
- Oh!

313
00:14:03,718 --> 00:14:05,719
- Angus?
- Yeah?

314
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:08,138
Uh, can I talk
to you outside?

315
00:14:08,139 --> 00:14:09,474
Yeah.

316
00:14:11,684 --> 00:14:14,354
So I've been automatic
writing all night.

317
00:14:17,273 --> 00:14:18,941
You can understand
all of this?

318
00:14:18,942 --> 00:14:20,442
Yes.

319
00:14:20,443 --> 00:14:22,236
I mean, I can't speak or
understand the spoken language,

320
00:14:22,237 --> 00:14:23,737
but I think I can understand

321
00:14:23,738 --> 00:14:25,656
enough of the written language
to be able to communicate

322
00:14:25,657 --> 00:14:28,367
with the people in the caves.

323
00:14:28,368 --> 00:14:31,203
So we have to go
back to the caves.

324
00:14:31,204 --> 00:14:32,621
Why?

325
00:14:32,622 --> 00:14:34,540
What if you were
right all along?

326
00:14:34,541 --> 00:14:36,291
Maybe they're trying
to tell us something.

327
00:14:36,292 --> 00:14:38,335
Okay, just let me
get a security detail

328
00:14:38,336 --> 00:14:40,421
together to go with us and--
- No.

329
00:14:40,422 --> 00:14:42,047
If we bring a bunch
of strangers down there,

330
00:14:42,048 --> 00:14:44,008
the people down there
might not let us in.

331
00:14:44,009 --> 00:14:46,927
Okay, but we should at least
tell Mr. Trust and Felix.

332
00:14:46,928 --> 00:14:48,512
I don't think we should.

333
00:14:48,513 --> 00:14:50,265
They'll never let us go alone.

334
00:14:51,766 --> 00:14:56,770
So you're saying you wanna
go, just us, no weapons,

335
00:14:56,771 --> 00:15:00,065
to see the people
who kidnapped us?

336
00:15:00,066 --> 00:15:02,568
Yes.

337
00:15:02,569 --> 00:15:05,947
I mean, I can always turn
my implants on if I have to.

338
00:15:08,950 --> 00:15:10,325
Hey, Dr. Kabir?

339
00:15:10,326 --> 00:15:12,286
Could I have a word?

340
00:15:12,287 --> 00:15:13,454
Um--

341
00:15:13,455 --> 00:15:15,289
It's private.

342
00:15:15,290 --> 00:15:16,958
Of course.

343
00:15:20,128 --> 00:15:21,587
What's wrong?

344
00:15:21,588 --> 00:15:24,340
I don't want to get
anyone in trouble.

345
00:15:24,341 --> 00:15:26,800
Okay.

346
00:15:26,801 --> 00:15:29,511
Whatever it is,
you can tell me.

347
00:15:32,265 --> 00:15:35,059
When Petrovic flatlined,

348
00:15:35,060 --> 00:15:38,103
Dr. Marsh hesitated--

349
00:15:38,104 --> 00:15:40,397
for too long.

350
00:15:40,398 --> 00:15:42,232
What do you mean hesitated?

351
00:15:42,233 --> 00:15:44,986
He just kind of
stood there, staring.

352
00:15:46,321 --> 00:15:48,614
Almost like he was
debating what to do.

353
00:15:48,615 --> 00:15:50,784
Then when I came over,
he snapped back to business.

354
00:15:52,911 --> 00:15:56,330
You did the right
thing telling me,

355
00:15:56,331 --> 00:15:59,792
but can we keep this
between us?

356
00:15:59,793 --> 00:16:01,168
Of course.

357
00:16:01,169 --> 00:16:02,336
Thank you.

358
00:16:24,734 --> 00:16:25,984
Clear.

359
00:16:58,476 --> 00:16:59,893
How did you find me?

360
00:16:59,894 --> 00:17:01,478
Put your gun down,
and we'll tell you.

361
00:17:07,068 --> 00:17:08,777
We just wanna talk.

362
00:17:08,778 --> 00:17:10,571
Okay?

363
00:17:18,079 --> 00:17:21,332
It's just that--

364
00:17:21,333 --> 00:17:22,458
I don't trust you.

365
00:17:34,429 --> 00:17:35,721
Hand over your unit beacon.

366
00:17:35,722 --> 00:17:37,182
Now.

367
00:17:39,476 --> 00:17:40,935
Kimi?

368
00:17:53,073 --> 00:17:56,241
What happened to
"Once a Thorn, always a Thorn?"

369
00:18:04,417 --> 00:18:07,920
Who's in
your Thorn unit, Ves?

370
00:18:07,921 --> 00:18:10,006
I don't know what
you're talking about.

371
00:18:12,133 --> 00:18:13,885
Then rot in here.

372
00:18:15,887 --> 00:18:17,389
Let's go.

373
00:18:23,978 --> 00:18:25,521
Well, that was successful.

374
00:18:25,522 --> 00:18:27,356
How are we gonna find
the rest of them now?

375
00:18:27,357 --> 00:18:28,900
I have an idea.

376
00:18:30,276 --> 00:18:32,736
You really think
Milan was Black Thorn?

377
00:18:32,737 --> 00:18:34,446
Well, he was close to Ves.

378
00:18:34,447 --> 00:18:37,324
Um, okay, but why
do you need me here?

379
00:18:37,325 --> 00:18:39,243
We're looking
for a beacon they carry.

380
00:18:39,244 --> 00:18:42,330
It's relatively small, gray,
and shaped kind of like--

381
00:18:44,582 --> 00:18:46,709
Kind of like this.

382
00:18:46,710 --> 00:18:48,085
It's password protected.

383
00:18:48,086 --> 00:18:49,461
That's why you're here, Sanji.

384
00:18:49,462 --> 00:18:52,090
Four digits,
using 1 through 6.

385
00:18:55,885 --> 00:19:00,764
Try 6161.

386
00:19:00,765 --> 00:19:02,599
It's the address
of his first house.

387
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:04,393
61--

388
00:19:04,394 --> 00:19:05,686
nope.

389
00:19:05,687 --> 00:19:06,895
Okay.

390
00:19:06,896 --> 00:19:09,190
Um--hmm.

391
00:19:10,775 --> 00:19:13,527
Try 1122.

392
00:19:13,528 --> 00:19:15,571
November 22nd.

393
00:19:15,572 --> 00:19:19,450
Month and day he was
sworn in as a cop.

394
00:19:19,451 --> 00:19:21,285
His proudest moment.

395
00:19:26,041 --> 00:19:27,958
Thank you, Sanji.

396
00:19:40,722 --> 00:19:42,765
I don't think there's
a way to disable the chip

397
00:19:42,766 --> 00:19:44,350
without killing Brice.

398
00:19:44,351 --> 00:19:46,101
Maybe if we can
figure out how

399
00:19:46,102 --> 00:19:48,937
the programming got into
his chip in the first place--

400
00:19:48,938 --> 00:19:50,189
It was that thing
that was connected

401
00:19:50,190 --> 00:19:52,274
behind my ear on Ross.
- Shut up.

402
00:19:52,275 --> 00:19:54,777
There's nothing on the MRI
where the tube was connected.

403
00:19:54,778 --> 00:19:55,736
It's just scar tissue.

404
00:19:59,407 --> 00:20:01,659
Or maybe it's not.

405
00:20:01,660 --> 00:20:02,701
Okay, okay.

406
00:20:02,702 --> 00:20:03,994
Look, I get it.

407
00:20:03,995 --> 00:20:06,413
You're mad I made you
go into the woods

408
00:20:06,414 --> 00:20:08,874
and try to hurt
your girlfriend.

409
00:20:08,875 --> 00:20:12,086
But I am doing
what I have to do.

410
00:20:12,087 --> 00:20:13,337
What's that?

411
00:20:13,338 --> 00:20:15,089
It's a bioelectric
impedance probe.

412
00:20:15,090 --> 00:20:17,049
Okay, what's it for?

413
00:20:17,050 --> 00:20:19,010
Well, if I'm correct...

414
00:20:21,638 --> 00:20:23,138
The scar tissue is conductive.

415
00:20:23,139 --> 00:20:24,765
- Shit.
- What?

416
00:20:24,766 --> 00:20:26,100
It's not scar tissue.

417
00:20:26,101 --> 00:20:28,102
It's some sort of
electro-organic strand

418
00:20:28,103 --> 00:20:29,311
that was left there
by the thing that

419
00:20:29,312 --> 00:20:31,021
connected behind Brice's ear.

420
00:20:31,022 --> 00:20:32,690
So this is how we can
access the chip?

421
00:20:32,691 --> 00:20:34,525
Exactly.

422
00:20:34,526 --> 00:20:36,611
Start rigging a contact.

423
00:20:38,697 --> 00:20:40,614
This isn't just about me.

424
00:20:40,615 --> 00:20:45,370
Trust me, if they disappear me,
you will never be the same.

425
00:20:47,789 --> 00:20:50,958
Do you have any plan
on how to get inside?

426
00:20:50,959 --> 00:20:53,377
I was sort of hoping
they would just--

427
00:20:58,925 --> 00:21:00,884
Do that.

428
00:21:27,912 --> 00:21:30,247
It's my clothes.

429
00:21:30,248 --> 00:21:33,043
Maybe it's
a gesture of goodwill?

430
00:21:42,886 --> 00:21:45,054
It means hello.

431
00:21:45,055 --> 00:21:46,598
I think.

432
00:22:32,394 --> 00:22:34,145
I don't like this.

433
00:22:36,981 --> 00:22:38,774
Come on.

434
00:23:14,310 --> 00:23:16,520
- Hey.
- Hmm.

435
00:23:16,521 --> 00:23:18,147
How's it going with Brice?

436
00:23:18,148 --> 00:23:20,691
It's complicated.

437
00:23:20,692 --> 00:23:22,943
What can I do to help?

438
00:23:22,944 --> 00:23:24,612
Nothing.

439
00:23:25,905 --> 00:23:27,698
Okay, Sanji.

440
00:23:27,699 --> 00:23:29,241
What's going on?

441
00:23:29,242 --> 00:23:31,035
You've been
avoiding me all day.

442
00:23:31,036 --> 00:23:33,662
I can't do this right now.

443
00:23:33,663 --> 00:23:34,913
Do what?

444
00:23:40,670 --> 00:23:41,879
Okay.

445
00:23:41,880 --> 00:23:43,464
If it's because
of what I said about Milan--

446
00:23:43,465 --> 00:23:44,757
It's not what you said.

447
00:23:44,758 --> 00:23:48,303
It's what you did,
or didn't do.

448
00:23:49,471 --> 00:23:51,013
What are you talking about?

449
00:24:00,690 --> 00:24:02,525
You killed him.

450
00:24:05,695 --> 00:24:07,279
No, I didn't.

451
00:24:07,280 --> 00:24:10,240
I checked
the medical records.

452
00:24:10,241 --> 00:24:14,536
Milan flatlined,
and you waited 12 seconds

453
00:24:14,537 --> 00:24:16,872
before trying to resuscitate.

454
00:24:16,873 --> 00:24:18,707
12 seconds.

455
00:24:18,708 --> 00:24:21,251
I was trying to be thoughtful
about the plan of action--

456
00:24:21,252 --> 00:24:22,503
Bullshit!

457
00:24:22,504 --> 00:24:24,756
You knew exactly
what was gonna happen.

458
00:24:27,467 --> 00:24:29,385
Even if I hadn't waited,

459
00:24:29,386 --> 00:24:32,262
it probably wouldn't have
made a difference.

460
00:24:32,263 --> 00:24:35,182
What the hell
kind of argument is that?

461
00:24:35,183 --> 00:24:37,519
I didn't mean for him to die.

462
00:24:38,937 --> 00:24:40,689
But you're not sorry.

463
00:24:44,150 --> 00:24:45,693
No.

464
00:24:45,694 --> 00:24:47,277
No, I'm not.

465
00:25:01,418 --> 00:25:03,377
Thanks for coming.

466
00:25:03,378 --> 00:25:05,004
Yeah, the water in that
lake was near freezing,

467
00:25:05,005 --> 00:25:07,464
so it preserved
the bodies fairly well.

468
00:25:07,465 --> 00:25:08,716
I was able to pull up
the manifest

469
00:25:08,717 --> 00:25:10,634
from the server we recovered.

470
00:25:10,635 --> 00:25:14,555
So we've been able to identify
most of them, but...

471
00:25:14,556 --> 00:25:17,225
we still need you to try
and ID the rest.

472
00:25:18,768 --> 00:25:23,188
I'm really sorry you have
to be the one to do this, but--

473
00:25:23,189 --> 00:25:24,940
Who else would do it?

474
00:25:42,584 --> 00:25:44,836
Lieutenant Efram Womby.

475
00:26:03,855 --> 00:26:06,858
Corporal Albert Flink.

476
00:26:30,215 --> 00:26:32,717
Leonard...

477
00:26:35,178 --> 00:26:36,888
Avega.

478
00:26:44,896 --> 00:26:46,397
My son.

479
00:27:09,504 --> 00:27:10,714
Can I join you?

480
00:27:22,058 --> 00:27:24,227
I'm so sorry about your son.

481
00:27:27,564 --> 00:27:30,441
I really wanted to blame you.

482
00:27:30,442 --> 00:27:32,609
Or at least the GSA.

483
00:27:32,610 --> 00:27:36,072
But the truth is,
it's my fault.

484
00:27:38,783 --> 00:27:41,744
Leo was an artist.

485
00:27:41,745 --> 00:27:44,955
He was happy

486
00:27:44,956 --> 00:27:48,000
painting alone in his room,

487
00:27:48,001 --> 00:27:49,793
even when the world was--

488
00:27:49,794 --> 00:27:52,379
was crumbling.

489
00:27:52,380 --> 00:27:58,177
He wasn't like me or anyone
I knew, for that matter.

490
00:27:58,178 --> 00:28:00,180
I couldn't understand him.

491
00:28:02,724 --> 00:28:03,933
I'm not a parent.

492
00:28:06,686 --> 00:28:08,730
Hell, I didn't
even have parents.

493
00:28:10,315 --> 00:28:12,107
But isn't that how
most parents feel,

494
00:28:12,108 --> 00:28:14,276
like they don't
understand their kids?

495
00:28:14,277 --> 00:28:16,445
Hmm.

496
00:28:16,446 --> 00:28:21,241
My wife always said
I was too hard on him.

497
00:28:21,242 --> 00:28:22,993
Your wife?

498
00:28:22,994 --> 00:28:27,290
Sheila, the love of my life.

499
00:28:28,666 --> 00:28:31,710
She died when Leo was 12.

500
00:28:31,711 --> 00:28:36,216
And I was left to raise
a boy I didn't understand.

501
00:28:37,759 --> 00:28:40,511
I am so sorry.

502
00:28:40,512 --> 00:28:43,889
I pushed him to join the EF,

503
00:28:43,890 --> 00:28:46,392
practically forced him.

504
00:28:46,393 --> 00:28:50,688
Told him he had to help
make a difference,

505
00:28:50,689 --> 00:28:52,314
and he hated me for it.

506
00:28:52,315 --> 00:28:53,649
I doubt that.

507
00:28:53,650 --> 00:28:55,192
Oh, no, he did.

508
00:28:55,193 --> 00:28:58,153
And because he hated me,
I assigned him

509
00:28:58,154 --> 00:29:01,532
to "EF1" instead of my ship,

510
00:29:01,533 --> 00:29:04,244
so I didn't have to
look him in the eye.

511
00:29:07,163 --> 00:29:08,580
And now--

512
00:29:08,581 --> 00:29:11,041
Zed, hey.

513
00:29:11,042 --> 00:29:13,127
His death is not your fault.

514
00:29:13,128 --> 00:29:15,546
I was his father.

515
00:29:15,547 --> 00:29:17,131
It was my job to protect him.

516
00:29:17,132 --> 00:29:19,258
You did protect him.

517
00:29:19,259 --> 00:29:21,510
If you hadn't put him on "EF1,"

518
00:29:21,511 --> 00:29:23,429
he probably would have died
two years earlier

519
00:29:23,430 --> 00:29:25,431
with everyone else
left behind on Earth.

520
00:29:25,432 --> 00:29:27,725
I should've put him
on "EF2" with me.

521
00:29:27,726 --> 00:29:30,310
He'd still be alive.

522
00:29:30,311 --> 00:29:33,564
You could not have
predicted what would happen.

523
00:29:33,565 --> 00:29:35,357
His death is not your fault.

524
00:29:35,358 --> 00:29:38,527
Then who the hell's
fault is it?

525
00:29:49,998 --> 00:29:52,833
James, there is still time
to stop this.

526
00:29:52,834 --> 00:29:55,169
Okay, this wire
can transmit signals

527
00:29:55,170 --> 00:29:56,587
to and from your
conductive tissue

528
00:29:56,588 --> 00:29:59,214
to access whatever
programming's in the chip.

529
00:29:59,215 --> 00:30:00,383
Buddy.

530
00:30:02,427 --> 00:30:03,636
Okay, try now.

531
00:30:05,555 --> 00:30:06,764
I'm in.

532
00:30:06,765 --> 00:30:07,973
I saved your life.

533
00:30:07,974 --> 00:30:09,808
Don't you owe me the same?

534
00:30:09,809 --> 00:30:10,851
It worked?

535
00:30:10,852 --> 00:30:13,520
Uh, well, sort of.

536
00:30:13,521 --> 00:30:14,855
I can see the code,

537
00:30:14,856 --> 00:30:17,775
but I can't
recognize it at all.

538
00:30:17,776 --> 00:30:19,610
What do you mean?

539
00:30:19,611 --> 00:30:20,819
It's not binary.

540
00:30:20,820 --> 00:30:21,820
It's ternary.

541
00:30:21,821 --> 00:30:23,280
Base three.

542
00:30:23,281 --> 00:30:24,907
I can't make sense of it.

543
00:30:24,908 --> 00:30:28,869
It's--it's totally foreign.

544
00:30:42,550 --> 00:30:44,718
What are you asking?

545
00:30:44,719 --> 00:30:46,387
I asked his name.

546
00:30:46,388 --> 00:30:49,056
But I can't translate
his response.

547
00:30:49,057 --> 00:30:51,267
Guess we'll just keep
calling him John Doe.

548
00:30:54,062 --> 00:30:56,523
How do you communicate
with each other?

549
00:31:08,201 --> 00:31:10,786
He says he spoke to them.

550
00:31:10,787 --> 00:31:13,288
But I didn't hear anything.

551
00:31:13,289 --> 00:31:17,042
They must talk in a frequency
outside our hearing range.

552
00:31:17,043 --> 00:31:18,335
It kind of makes sense.

553
00:31:18,336 --> 00:31:20,964
He has different
hearing and vocal cords.

554
00:31:22,132 --> 00:31:24,508
Ask them why we were kidnapped.

555
00:31:46,031 --> 00:31:48,157
"You break."

556
00:31:48,158 --> 00:31:50,200
You break what?

557
00:31:50,201 --> 00:31:51,660
It's that symbol.

558
00:31:51,661 --> 00:31:53,455
It's the only one
I can't translate.

559
00:31:59,044 --> 00:32:01,004
What does it mean?

560
00:32:37,415 --> 00:32:40,001
Did you trigger it?
- No.

561
00:32:47,926 --> 00:32:49,177
Who made the call?

562
00:33:12,033 --> 00:33:13,909
- Against the wall!
- Masks off.

563
00:33:13,910 --> 00:33:15,953
And keep your hands
where we can see them.

564
00:33:24,879 --> 00:33:26,714
Okay, I've combed through
everything on the chip.

565
00:33:26,715 --> 00:33:28,716
The code is indecipherable.

566
00:33:28,717 --> 00:33:31,427
But if we can purge
the code from the chip,

567
00:33:31,428 --> 00:33:34,388
there may be a chance that
Brice will go back to normal.

568
00:33:34,389 --> 00:33:36,390
"Purge" means I will be gone.

569
00:33:36,391 --> 00:33:37,975
Do you understand?

570
00:33:37,976 --> 00:33:41,812
Guys, maybe we shouldn't
delete it all, you know?

571
00:33:41,813 --> 00:33:43,647
We might need
the information later.

572
00:33:43,648 --> 00:33:44,732
Yeah, that's true.

573
00:33:44,733 --> 00:33:46,233
With all
these questions looming

574
00:33:46,234 --> 00:33:48,569
about Ross and Homebase,
it could be valuable.

575
00:33:48,570 --> 00:33:49,987
I am valuable.

576
00:33:49,988 --> 00:33:54,033
But I'm of no use to you
if I'm not in your head.

577
00:33:54,034 --> 00:33:55,200
You're right.

578
00:33:55,201 --> 00:33:57,369
Instead of purging it,
I'll move the data

579
00:33:57,370 --> 00:33:58,912
into an air-gapped device.

580
00:33:58,913 --> 00:34:01,248
That way it can't infiltrate
our computer system.

581
00:34:01,249 --> 00:34:02,875
But the software will
be completely

582
00:34:02,876 --> 00:34:04,585
out of his head, right?

583
00:34:04,586 --> 00:34:06,420
Right.
It'll be here instead.

584
00:34:06,421 --> 00:34:07,921
Please.

585
00:34:07,922 --> 00:34:10,257
James, you don't know
what you're doing.

586
00:34:10,258 --> 00:34:12,551
Alicia...

587
00:34:12,552 --> 00:34:14,136
do it.

588
00:34:14,137 --> 00:34:16,180
James.

589
00:34:16,181 --> 00:34:17,723
James, please.

590
00:34:30,028 --> 00:34:31,612
You will regret this.

591
00:34:34,449 --> 00:34:36,241
This is for the best.

592
00:34:36,242 --> 00:34:37,326
Who is he talking to?

593
00:34:37,327 --> 00:34:38,369
I don't know.

594
00:34:38,370 --> 00:34:42,624
I will make you regret this.

595
00:34:44,125 --> 00:34:45,126
Goodbye.

596
00:34:49,798 --> 00:34:52,383
The transfer is complete.

597
00:34:52,384 --> 00:34:54,093
How do you feel, James?

598
00:34:58,556 --> 00:35:00,809
I, uh--

599
00:35:02,227 --> 00:35:03,645
Thank you.

600
00:35:10,068 --> 00:35:12,195
Just let him rest.
Let him rest.

601
00:35:16,574 --> 00:35:18,283
Here's how it's gonna go.

602
00:35:18,284 --> 00:35:22,746
You're going to tell us exactly
what happened two years ago.

603
00:35:22,747 --> 00:35:25,207
The only way
I'm telling you anything

604
00:35:25,208 --> 00:35:27,960
is if you let my team go.

605
00:35:27,961 --> 00:35:29,628
They were only
following orders.

606
00:35:29,629 --> 00:35:31,839
Absolutely not.

607
00:35:31,840 --> 00:35:34,049
But I can promise you this.

608
00:35:34,050 --> 00:35:36,719
If you don't help us right now,

609
00:35:36,720 --> 00:35:39,430
your team will suffer
grave consequences.

610
00:35:39,431 --> 00:35:42,934
Okay.

611
00:35:44,477 --> 00:35:48,273
Ves, we can't make a deal until
we know exactly what happened.

612
00:35:51,526 --> 00:35:54,111
Fine.

613
00:35:54,112 --> 00:35:55,739
Start talking.

614
00:35:56,990 --> 00:35:58,949
We killed those
"EF1" survivors.

615
00:35:58,950 --> 00:36:01,577
Avega, you have to understand
that, at that time,

616
00:36:01,578 --> 00:36:03,996
they were still the enemy.

617
00:36:03,997 --> 00:36:06,165
We were in the fog of war.

618
00:36:07,459 --> 00:36:09,960
<i>The mission was standard--</i>

619
00:36:09,961 --> 00:36:12,379
<i>do a sweep and make sure
there were no hostiles here</i>

620
00:36:12,380 --> 00:36:14,549
<i>before "Ark 11" came down.</i>

621
00:36:15,508 --> 00:36:19,970
We were about to turn around
and go back to the ship

622
00:36:19,971 --> 00:36:22,097
when we smelled smoke.

623
00:36:22,098 --> 00:36:23,141
Smoke?

624
00:36:25,351 --> 00:36:26,685
Camp smoke.

625
00:36:30,857 --> 00:36:33,067
<i>We followed it</i>

626
00:36:33,068 --> 00:36:36,237
<i>and found a group of people
living in the woods somehow.</i>

627
00:36:41,201 --> 00:36:43,077
They're EF.

628
00:36:43,078 --> 00:36:44,411
Fire!

629
00:37:01,763 --> 00:37:04,431
So you just killed
all those people?

630
00:37:04,432 --> 00:37:05,766
We were outnumbered.

631
00:37:05,767 --> 00:37:06,850
They were going to kill us--

632
00:37:06,851 --> 00:37:08,560
You do not know that!

633
00:37:08,561 --> 00:37:10,312
Avega, please.

634
00:37:10,313 --> 00:37:12,356
Why didn't you tell us
any of this before?

635
00:37:12,357 --> 00:37:14,441
Why murder Hammond
to keep this secret?

636
00:37:14,442 --> 00:37:17,027
Because of you two,
Sharon and Zed.

637
00:37:17,028 --> 00:37:18,737
- Oh, come on.
- Wait, me?

638
00:37:18,738 --> 00:37:21,115
When you came here,
you had made peace.

639
00:37:21,116 --> 00:37:23,951
I wasn't going to blow it
by revealing who we had killed.

640
00:37:23,952 --> 00:37:25,369
No, it doesn't
make any sense.

641
00:37:25,370 --> 00:37:26,620
You buried the bodies.

642
00:37:26,621 --> 00:37:28,205
You wanted to cover it up
right away.

643
00:37:28,206 --> 00:37:30,374
Weapons.

644
00:37:30,375 --> 00:37:31,750
What?

645
00:37:31,751 --> 00:37:33,293
There were
no weapons recovered

646
00:37:33,294 --> 00:37:34,753
from that pile of bodies.

647
00:37:37,716 --> 00:37:40,634
The EF soldiers
were unarmed

648
00:37:40,635 --> 00:37:42,137
when you found them,
weren't they?

649
00:37:44,014 --> 00:37:49,309
You mowed down
all those unarmed people?

650
00:37:49,310 --> 00:37:52,521
I wanna know how
you shot down "EF1,"

651
00:37:52,522 --> 00:37:55,691
how you killed hundreds
of innocent people

652
00:37:55,692 --> 00:37:56,775
on board that ship.

653
00:37:56,776 --> 00:37:58,068
Tell me!

654
00:37:58,069 --> 00:38:00,195
I didn't--I didn't know
anything about that.

655
00:38:00,196 --> 00:38:01,280
Avega!

656
00:38:01,281 --> 00:38:02,406
You're a liar!

657
00:38:05,327 --> 00:38:06,952
She is a murderer.

658
00:38:06,953 --> 00:38:09,331
Yes, she is.

659
00:38:11,583 --> 00:38:13,751
But don't let her
turn you into one.

660
00:38:33,605 --> 00:38:36,815
Ian, if you've come
to try and calm me down--

661
00:38:36,816 --> 00:38:39,026
No, no, no. No.

662
00:38:39,027 --> 00:38:41,362
Just to give you
some information.

663
00:38:41,363 --> 00:38:44,073
The server shut down
two weeks before

664
00:38:44,074 --> 00:38:45,825
"Ark 11" arrived at Homebase.

665
00:38:47,702 --> 00:38:49,828
I'm not sure I follow.

666
00:38:49,829 --> 00:38:52,873
The server shut down
because the ship went down

667
00:38:52,874 --> 00:38:55,710
before Ves or "Ark 11"
were even here.

668
00:38:57,670 --> 00:38:59,546
So Ves was telling the truth.

669
00:39:03,885 --> 00:39:07,137
I don't know
who shot down "EF1,"

670
00:39:07,138 --> 00:39:08,972
but it wasn't her.

671
00:39:13,937 --> 00:39:16,146
You're saying you've
been seeing and hearing

672
00:39:16,147 --> 00:39:18,023
Doc Morozov this whole time?

673
00:39:18,024 --> 00:39:19,733
Yep.

674
00:39:19,734 --> 00:39:21,694
Thanks.

675
00:39:21,695 --> 00:39:23,195
Yeah.

676
00:39:23,196 --> 00:39:25,406
And she felt so real.

677
00:39:25,407 --> 00:39:28,242
That must've been some
insanely advanced AI.

678
00:39:28,243 --> 00:39:29,868
- Mm.
- Yeah.

679
00:39:29,869 --> 00:39:31,453
Yep.

680
00:39:31,454 --> 00:39:33,539
She saved my life.

681
00:39:33,540 --> 00:39:36,875
Made it seem like I was
supposed to save her too.

682
00:39:36,876 --> 00:39:41,088
Something about, like, fixing
a part of her here on Homebase.

683
00:39:41,089 --> 00:39:42,881
A part of her?
What does that mean?

684
00:39:42,882 --> 00:39:44,341
I don't know.

685
00:39:44,342 --> 00:39:45,843
Never got that far.

686
00:39:49,180 --> 00:39:51,765
Oh, man, I am just so, so happy

687
00:39:51,766 --> 00:39:54,101
to feel like myself again,
you know?

688
00:39:54,102 --> 00:39:57,312
Thank you, both of you,
for everything, really.

689
00:39:57,313 --> 00:39:58,939
I'm so happy you're okay.

690
00:39:58,940 --> 00:40:00,107
Oh, oh, okay.

691
00:40:00,108 --> 00:40:02,901
You're friendly.

692
00:40:02,902 --> 00:40:04,028
One of the new doctors.

693
00:40:04,029 --> 00:40:05,195
Yeah.

694
00:40:05,196 --> 00:40:06,864
Uh, we haven't met, have we?

695
00:40:06,865 --> 00:40:07,948
I'm James.

696
00:40:07,949 --> 00:40:09,074
James Brice.

697
00:40:09,075 --> 00:40:10,993
Nice to meet you.

698
00:40:10,994 --> 00:40:12,953
Um--

699
00:40:15,999 --> 00:40:17,666
What?

700
00:40:17,667 --> 00:40:19,293
So Ves didn't
shoot down the ship.

701
00:40:19,294 --> 00:40:20,669
No, she couldn't have.

702
00:40:20,670 --> 00:40:24,257
I despise her,
but she didn't kill my boy.

703
00:40:25,884 --> 00:40:28,594
What happens when we meet
the people who did?

704
00:40:28,595 --> 00:40:31,388
I think we already have.

705
00:40:31,389 --> 00:40:33,515
There's only one group
of people that could have

706
00:40:33,516 --> 00:40:36,477
been here when "EF1" arrived.

707
00:40:36,478 --> 00:40:37,978
The people in the caves.

708
00:40:37,979 --> 00:40:39,271
Wait.

709
00:40:39,272 --> 00:40:42,816
If they were able to
shoot down a spaceship, then--

710
00:40:42,817 --> 00:40:45,819
They must have access
to a massive weapon.

711
00:40:53,787 --> 00:40:55,537
Fix?

712
00:40:55,538 --> 00:40:57,415
I don't understand.

713
00:41:05,965 --> 00:41:08,342
Heal.

714
00:41:08,343 --> 00:41:10,052
Fix what? Heal what?

715
00:41:10,053 --> 00:41:11,513
I don't know.

716
00:41:30,990 --> 00:41:32,367
Fix or death.

717
00:41:34,703 --> 00:41:35,911
Hey.

718
00:41:50,343 --> 00:41:51,969
Is he saying--

719
00:41:51,970 --> 00:41:54,973
If we don't fix it,
they'll kill us.

